Scope of this license

The MIT license above applies ONLY to the project's own original scripts,
recipes, and configuration files written for Lumenora. These are:

  - the BlueBuild recipes under `recipes/`
  - the build scripts under `files/scripts/` and `scripts/`
  - the customization/configuration files under `files/` (skel dotfiles,
    MangoHud/GameMode configs, Lumen Plasma theme, wallpapers, systemd units,
    the GPU-detection tooling under `files/usr/`)
  - the `Containerfile`, `installer/` definitions, and the GitHub Actions
    workflows under `.github/`

All other software bundled into or referenced by Lumenora is NOT covered by
the MIT license above. Lumenora is an ostree/bootc image built on top of
Fedora Atomic Desktop (Kinoite) and aggregates many independent, separately
licensed components. Those components remain governed by their own licenses:

  - Fedora / the kernel and core system: GPL-2.0 (or later) and the Fedora
    licensing policy.
  - The Linux kernel is under GPL-2.0-only; any GPL components you build or
    ship as part of a distribution of Lumenora must be redistributed in
    compliance with their respective GPL obligations.
  - KDE Plasma, KDE Gear, and Qt are under the LGPL-2.1-or-later / GPL-2.0-
    or-later / GFDL family of licenses.
  - The Open Game Collective (OGC) gaming kernel is a derived kernel and is
    GPL-2.0.
  - NVIDIA driver rpms, akmods builds, and nvidia-container-toolkit packages
    are under the NVIDIA license and applicable open-source licenses; they
    are redistributed by the installation process, not by this project.
  - All other packaged applications, libraries, and binary components keep
    their upstream licenses.

This image is built and redistributed in accordance with Fedora's legal
guidelines. Users are responsible for ensuring that any redistribution of
the image or its binaries complies with the individual licenses of the
included components, including GNU GPL copyleft obligations.